  "reason": "The current best (config_013, acc=0.713) uses scvi_n200 as the RNA encoder in a multiprofile + transformer + weighted-fusion architecture. The only RNA encoder tested in this top architecture is scvi_n200, leaving a critical uncertainty: does the choice of learned RNA representation matter? Since RNA is the dominant signal source (rna_only multiprofile+transformer = 0.653 vs image_only = 0.208), the RNA encoder is likely the highest-leverage design choice remaining. config_042 (scgpt, resnet50, transformer, weighted, multiprofile, multimodal) changes only the RNA encoder from scvi_n200 to scgpt while holding all other settings identical to config_013, giving a clean A/B comparison. If scgpt matches or exceeds scvi_n200, it broadens the viable encoder space; if it underperforms, it confirms scvi_n200's advantage and redirects budget toward image-encoder or other factors. This is the most informative single-variable experiment under the limited budget."
}

